{
	default_hide_dependency_lines: false
	default_quest_shape: ""
	filename: "create_electric"
	group: "1A2B000000000006"
	icon: "createaddition:alternator"
	id: "5E1F000000000000"
	order_index: 0
	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"&e&lYou have torque. Mekanism wants amps.&r"
				""
				"Every machine from here on runs on &eFE&r - Forge Energy - and Create does not make any. The Kinetic Age gave you rotation; this chapter converts it."
				""
				"&e&lFE and SU are nothing alike, and mixing them up will cost you hours:&r"
				"&7- &fSU&7 is a &lbudget&r&7. It is not stored, not consumed, and not transported. Add a machine, spend capacity. Remove it, get the capacity back."
				"&7- &fFE&7 is a &lquantity&r&7. It is generated, stored in a buffer, moved down a wire, and used up. Run out and things stop until you make more."
				""
				"The &eAlternator&r is the bridge. Spin it and it produces FE - faster rotation, more FE, up to its cap. It draws SU from your network to do it, so a big alternator bank needs a matching water wheel bank behind it."
				""
				"&8This is the smallest possible answer to \"how do I power a Metallurgic Infuser\". Everything else in this chapter is refinement."
			]
			icon: "createaddition:alternator"
			id: "5E10000000000001"
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Where FE comes from"
			tasks: [{
				id: "59EEBE7A7497A16C"
				item: "createaddition:alternator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6Rotation Into Electricity"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5E10000000000001"]
			description: [
				"FE does not flow through thin air. You need a &eConnector&r on the machine that makes it, another on the machine that wants it, and &eWire&r between."
				""
				"&e&lThree wires, three throughputs:&r"
				"&7- &fCopper&7 - cheap, lowest transfer rate. Fine near your generators."
				"&7- &fGold&7 - middle."
				"&7- &fElectrum&7 - the good stuff. Gold plus silver in a mixer."
				""
				"&e&lTwo connector sizes.&r The plain &eConnector&r handles ordinary loads. The &eLarge Connector&r moves far more per tick and is what you want between a generator bank and a machine room."
				""
				"&7Wire is placed by right-clicking one connector then the other - it strings across the gap and does not care about the blocks in between. Long runs are free. That is a genuine advantage over pipes.&r"
			]
			icon: "createaddition:connector"
			id: "5E10000000000002"
			subtitle: "&7Getting FE from A to B"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "552E92FBF8763929"
					item: "createaddition:connector"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "05A5D23E778A8400"
					item: "createaddition:copper_wire"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6Wires and Connectors"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5E10000000000002"]
			description: [
				"Generation is never perfectly steady and demand never perfectly flat. A &eCapacitor&r sits between them and absorbs the difference."
				""
				"&e&lWhy you want one immediately:&r a machine that briefly asks for more than your alternators produce will simply stall without a buffer. With one, it draws down the stored charge and carries on while generation catches up."
				""
				"&7Think of it as the difference between a tap and a water butt. The tap sets your long-run average; the butt covers the spikes.&r"
			]
			icon: "createaddition:capacitor"
			id: "5E10000000000003"
			subtitle: "&7A buffer, not a battery bank"
			tasks: [{
				id: "324D8CA3B11FE777"
				item: "createaddition:capacitor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6The Capacitor"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5E10000000000003"]
			description: [
				"A Capacitor smooths. An &eAccumulator&r &lstores&r."
				""
				"The &eModular Accumulator&r is the one that matters - place several in a rectangle and they merge into a single multiblock with pooled capacity. Bigger footprint, bigger reservoir, one connection point."
				""
				"&e&lBuild this before you think you need it.&r The moment you automate anything that runs in bursts - a furnace bank, an ore line, anything on a timer - you are relying on stored charge rather than instantaneous generation."
			]
			icon: "createaddition:accumulator"
			id: "5E10000000000004"
			subtitle: "&7Real storage"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3E7BACAFE6D0E0D8"
				item: "createaddition:accumulator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6The Accumulator"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5E10000000000004"]
			description: [
				"The &eElectric Motor&r is an Alternator in reverse: feed it FE and it outputs rotation."
				""
				"&e&lThis is more useful than it first sounds.&r It lets you run a Create contraption anywhere without dragging shafts to it - solar or a reactor on one side of the base, a motor next to the machine that needs turning on the other."
				""
				"&7Its speed is configurable with a wrench, which makes it a cleaner source than gearing down a water wheel when a machine needs one exact RPM.&r"
				""
				"&8Rotation to FE, FE to rotation. Once you have both, the two systems stop being separate and become one."
			]
			icon: "createaddition:electric_motor"
			id: "5E10000000000005"
			subtitle: "&7Back the other way"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4D05EEA05644794F"
				item: "createaddition:electric_motor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6The Electric Motor"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5E10000000000005"]
			description: [
				"A &eTesla Coil&r charges anything with a battery in it - inside a radius, with no connector and no wire."
				""
				"Put one in your base and every powered tool, jetpack and backpack you walk past tops itself up. It will also happily electrocute mobs that wander into range, which is a defence system you did not have to design."
				""
				"&7Pair it with the &eDigital Adapter&r if you want redstone to read the state of your electrical network - useful for switching generators on only when storage drops.&r"
			]
			icon: "createaddition:tesla_coil"
			id: "5E10000000000006"
			subtitle: "&7Charging without wires"
			tasks: [{
				id: "313A4EBA38938767"
				item: "createaddition:tesla_coil"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6The Tesla Coil"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5E10000000000006"]
			description: [
				"&6&lYou can now make, store, move and spend electricity.&r"
				""
				"That is the prerequisite for everything Act II asks of you. The Metallurgic Infuser, the Enrichment Chamber, the Crusher - all of them want FE and none of them care where it came from."
				""
				"&e&lTwo directions from here:&r"
				"&7- &fMekanism&7 - go and power the machines this chapter was built for."
				"&7- &fCreate Power Grid&7 - if you want electricity that behaves like real electricity, with voltage, transformers and circuits you etch yourself."
				""
				"&8Powah, Solar Flux and Advanced Generators are all later, larger answers to the same question. None of them is required to start Mekanism."
			]
			icon: "createaddition:electrum_wire"
			id: "5E10000000000007"
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "&7Act II can begin"
			tasks: [{
				id: "510F0B77D0BE1ED2"
				item: "createaddition:electrum_wire"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6Wired Up"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
	]
	subtitle: ["&7Turning rotation into FE"]
	title: "&6Create Crafts & Additions"
}
